INT. DRIVER'S LICENSE OFFICE - WAITING AREA - DAY

Plastic chairs bolted in rows. A take-a-number machine. A flag. A sign: PLEASE HAVE ALL DOCUMENTS READY.

ERNEST PLUMLEY (60s, bow tie, blazer with elbow patches, a folder of papers held in both hands) sits in the exact middle of the front row. He aligns his folder with the edge of his knee. He checks his watch. He checks his ticket: B-114. The overhead display reads B-103.

He squares his shoulders and stares at the display with immense confidence.

The display ticks. B-104.

He nods. He smiles at nobody. He pulls a small cassette recorder from his blazer pocket and presses record.

ERNEST
(into recorder)
Note to self. Today I renew my license. A calm man. A prepared man.

He clicks it off, pockets it, and checks the folder again, thumbing each page in order. His smile does not waver.

The display ticks. B-105.

His eyes flick to a bank of windows. A clerk, unseen, slams a stamp. Ernest flinches, covers it with a cough, and straightens his bow tie.

The display ticks. B-106. Ernest's knee begins to bounce. He holds his folder down with his free hand to still it.

He pulls out the recorder again. He presses play.

ERNEST (V.O.)
(recorded)
Note to self. Today I renew my license. A calm man. A prepared man.

He listens to his own voice, serene. He rewinds a few seconds and plays it again. He nods to it, as to a trusted colleague.

The display ticks. B-107. Ernest rises, tests his legs, sits again.

He opens his folder. He turns a page. He freezes. He turns another page, and another, faster. His face drains of color, one shade at a time.

He pulls out the recorder with trembling fingers.

ERNEST
(into recorder)
Note to self.

He stops. His lip works.

ERNEST (CONT'D)
(into recorder)
The proof of residence is on the kitchen table.

He clicks it off. He looks at the display. B-108. He looks at his ticket. B-114.

Slowly, with enormous dignity, he gets up, tucks the folder under his arm, and walks to the door. Halfway, he stops, turns, and returns to his seat, and sits, and folds his hands, and stares at the display with immense confidence.
